# **Section-by-Section Findings**

Findings ordered by severity within each section. Finding IDs (e.g. F3-004) are used for cross-referencing in the action plan. Sections with no findings are shown with a healthy marker.

## **Section 2: Governance, Budget, Staffing, and Ownership**

**[URGENT]  ****Emergency access methods and credentials not documented or controlled**  F2-007   ● Staff time only

There is no documented or controlled record of emergency access methods or shared credentials. Undocumented shared credentials are frequently identified as a root cause in costly IT failures.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify all shared credentials and emergency access methods currently in use.*  [Immediate]* **→  **Document, secure, and control access to these credentials — using a password manager, sealed physical record, or equivalent.*  [Within 30 days]* **→  **Verify that at least one other authorized person can access these credentials without involving the primary IT person.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****System ownership not documented**  F2-003   ● Moderate budget

There is no documented record of who owns or is accountable for major platforms and services.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Create a system ownership register listing each major platform, its owner, and the backup contact.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****Vendor contacts and escalation paths not documented**  F2-004   ● Moderate budget

There is no documented record of who to contact at key vendors when something goes wrong.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Create a vendor contact sheet listing each major vendor, support contact, contract or account number, and escalation path.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****Primary IT lead cannot be reliably covered if unavailable**  F2-008   ● Moderate budget

Basic IT operations could partially continue if the primary IT person were unavailable, but coverage is incomplete.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify at least one person who could cover basic IT operations in an emergency.*  [Within 90 days]* **→  **Document the minimum knowledge and access that person would need and begin cross-training.*  [Within 90 days]* **→  **Consider establishing a relationship with an MSP or IT consultant as a coverage backstop.*  [Within 12 months]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Known budget or staffing constraints affecting IT this year**  F2-006

The IT person has identified active constraints that will limit what can be accomplished this year. Recommendations that require significant spend or staff are flagged with a constraint marker.

| ***IT person noted: ****Budget is flat year-over-year; no new FTE approved for IT. Device refresh for grades 3-5 is funded but all other discretionary spend is under review.* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Recurring IT tasks only partially tracked**  F2-009   ● Staff time only

Some recurring IT tasks are tracked but the system is incomplete.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Complete the recurring IT task calendar or checklist.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

