## **Section 7: Data Protection, Backup, and Recovery**

**[URGENT]  ****Server backup coverage incomplete**  F7-004   ● Moderate budget

Some servers are backed up but others are not. Any unprotected server represents complete data loss risk.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Extend backup coverage to all servers.*  [Immediate]* |
| --- |

**[URGENT]  ****Backup restore not tested or not tested recently**  F7-008   ● Staff time only

A backup that has never been tested — or not tested within a timeframe proportional to the backup's useful recovery window — cannot be relied upon.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Schedule and perform a documented restore test for at least one critical system.*  [Within 30 days]* **→  **Establish a recurring restore test schedule aligned with the backup retention window.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[URGENT]  ****Emergency access to critical credentials not confirmed**  F7-012   ● Staff time only

Critical admin credentials and recovery materials are not confirmed to be accessible in an emergency. If the primary IT person is unavailable during an incident, recovery may be impossible.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify all critical admin credentials and recovery materials.*  [Immediate]* **→  **Store credentials securely in a documented, accessible location.*  [Within 30 days]* **→  **Verify that at least one other authorized person knows how to access these materials.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[URGENT]  ****Backups running but recovery confidence is low**  F7-C02   ● Staff time only

Backups appear to be in place but are not monitored reliably and have not been tested recently. The school may believe it is protected when it is not.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Perform an immediate backup review — confirm jobs are running, review success logs, and schedule a restore test.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****Backup success not regularly monitored**  F7-007   ● Staff time only

Backups may be running but are not reviewed for success. Silent backup failures are a common cause of data loss discovered only at the moment recovery is needed.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Establish a weekly backup review cadence.*  [Within 30 days]* **→  **Configure alerting so backup failures notify the IT person automatically.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****No defined recovery priority for critical systems**  F7-010   ● Staff time only

When multiple systems are affected in an incident, the order of recovery matters. Without a defined priority, decisions are made under pressure without a plan.

| **ℹ  Note: **This finding is harder to resolve because the environment currently lacks a central documentation system — addressing Section 9 findings first will make this and other documentation gaps easier to close systematically. |
| --- |

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Define and document a recovery priority order for critical systems.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****No written incident or disaster response reference**  F7-011   ● Staff time only

There is no documented reference for how to respond to a significant IT incident or outage. In a crisis, whoever is covering needs a written starting point. A one-page reference is sufficient.

| **ℹ  Note: **This finding is harder to resolve because the environment currently lacks a central documentation system — addressing Section 9 findings first will make this and other documentation gaps easier to close systematically. |
| --- |

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Create a basic IT incident response reference covering: who to call, what systems to check first, how to access backup and recovery tools, and how to communicate during an outage.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****Restore test frequency not aligned with backup retention window**  F7-014   ● Staff time only

The school knows how far back a restore is useful but is not testing frequently enough to detect failures within that window.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Establish a restore test schedule aligned with the useful recovery window — at least one test per window period.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Backup scope partially documented**  F7-002   ● Staff time only

Undocumented systems may not be protected.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Complete the backup scope documentation.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

## **Section 8: Security Operations, Filtering, and Safeguards**

**[CONCERN]  ****Known unresolved security concerns identified**  F8-008   ● Significant investment

The IT person has identified active, unresolved security concerns. These should be treated as immediate priorities.

| ***IT person noted: ****A staff laptop was reported missing last month — it is unclear if it was lost or stolen. The device was not encrypted and did not have remote wipe configured. This has not yet been formally reported or documented.* |
| --- |

| **ℹ  Note: **Identifying a known problem scores better than not knowing — you cannot fix what you are not aware of. |
| --- |

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Document each identified security concern with a description, estimated risk level, and a specific action and owner.*  [Immediate]* **→  **Address each confirmed concern according to its severity.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Endpoint protection alerts reviewed irregularly**  F8-001b   ● Staff time only

Alerts are reviewed occasionally. Threats may persist between reviews.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Establish a regular weekly alert review cadence.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Endpoint and server patching informal**  F8-002   ● Staff time only

Patching happens when the IT person is aware of a specific issue rather than on a schedule.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Define and document a patching schedule.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Network and security device firmware reviewed irregularly**  F8-003   ● Staff time only

Firmware is reviewed irregularly. Gaps between reviews represent periods where known vulnerabilities may be present.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Establish a twice-yearly firmware review cadence.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Student safety and filtering controls not documented**  F8-005   ● Staff time only

Controls are in place but not documented well enough to understand coverage and gaps.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Document the current filtering and student safety control configuration — what is filtered, who is covered, and what the exception process is.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Incident response process partially documented**  F8-006   ● Moderate budget

Key scenarios or steps may be missing.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Complete the incident response reference.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****System logs and alerts not regularly reviewed**  F8-007   ● Staff time only

Logs from key systems are not reviewed regularly. Security events go unnoticed until they become significant incidents.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Establish a monthly review of authentication logs, failed logins, and security alerts.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

## **Section 9: Documentation and Operational Readiness**

**[CONCERN]  ****IT environment only partially understandable from existing documentation**  F9-005   ● Moderate budget

The environment is only partially understandable. A third party could handle some situations but would be unable to support key areas without investigation.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify and document the areas where documentation is weakest.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[CONCERN]  ****Critical IT knowledge concentrated in a single person**  F9-006   ● Moderate budget

Major IT knowledge areas exist only in one person's head. If that person leaves, becomes ill, or is unavailable, the school loses access to that knowledge entirely.

| ***IT person noted: ****Firewall configuration — only the Director of Technology knows the full rule set and admin credentials. Phone system (8x8) — configuration history and admin portal access are not documented. Veeam backup jobs — only one person has ever logged into the management console.* |
| --- |

| **ℹ  Note: **Identifying and naming knowledge concentration areas earns partial credit — naming the gap is the first step to closing it. |
| --- |

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify each area of knowledge concentration and develop a documentation or cross-training plan for each.*  [Within 90 days]* **→  **Prioritize documentation of the highest-risk knowledge areas.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Some IT documentation outdated**  F9-002   ● Moderate budget

Most documentation is reasonably current but some areas lag.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify and update outdated documentation sections.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****SOPs documented for some but not all recurring tasks**  F9-003   ● Staff time only

Missing procedures represent tasks that cannot be delegated reliably.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Identify and document SOPs for the highest-risk undocumented recurring tasks.*  [Within 90 days]* |
| --- |

**[WATCH]  ****Change documentation process informal**  F9-004   ● Staff time only

Changes are sometimes documented informally.

| **Recommended actions:** **→  **Formalize the change documentation process.*  [Within 30 days]* |
| --- |

